Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.22,0:01:10.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the Kola superdeep borehole in Russia, some call it{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.05,0:01:13.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the gateway to hell, with locals claiming to hear the screams{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.73,0:01:17.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}of tortured souls. At around 30 to{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.73,0:01:20.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}50 km depth, we reach the next layer,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.56,0:01:23.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the mantle. It's made of hot rock,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.94,0:01:27.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}which appears solid to us, but actually flows very slowly,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.08,0:01:32.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}just a few centimeters a year. These delicate shifts below{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.25,0:01:36.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}can give rise to earthquakes above. In the 1960s,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.87,0:01:40.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}a group of scientists attempted to drill into{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.31,0:01:44.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the earth's mantle. Although unsuccessful, new efforts are afoot{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.50,0:01:47.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with a plan to drill deep below the Indian Ocean.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.52,0:01:51.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As we descend, the increasing pressure means{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.72,0:01:55.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that atoms become warped and even the most familiar materials{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.68,0:01:59.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}behave bizarrely. Crystals change from green to blue{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.66,0:02:03.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to brown, and rock becomes as malleable as plastic.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.98,0:02:07.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}2900 kilometers down, we reach{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.30,0:02:10.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the bottom of the mantle. See those two giant blobs?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.86,0:02:13.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They are the size of continents.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.50,0:02:16.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Scientists arent sure how they were formed or{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.90,0:02:19.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}what theyre made of. They cradle the next layer,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.84,0:02:23.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the outer core. In Jules Verne's classic{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.37,0:02:26.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}novel Journey to the center of the earth, Professor Otto Lydenbrock{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.95,0:02:30.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}encounters an entire underground world, replete with prehistoric{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.89,0:02:34.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}creatures and the subterranean ocean. While the dinosaurs{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.87,0:02:38.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}might have been a bit of a stretch, there is an ocean of sorts.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.53,0:02:41.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But this one consists of flowing red hot{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.90,0:02:45.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}iron and nickel, a sunless sea with its own currents{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.88,0:02:49.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and jet streams. This motion creates a magnetic field{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.00,0:02:53.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that protects the earth from dangerous solar rays.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.00,0:02:57.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The final layer is known as the inner core.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.45,0:03:00.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's 6000 degrees in here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.96,0:03:04.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The pressure is so intense that the{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.17,0:03:08.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}metals here have crystallized, forming a solid sphere{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.08,0:03:10.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}at the very center of our planet.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.40,0:03:16.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}In reality, our little vehicle would have been crushed and melted{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.62,0:03:19.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}long ago. And as for our driver, I think she better{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.03,0:03:23.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}head back to the surface. It's a long way to go.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.68,0:03:24.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Good luck.{\i0}
